  ('nb2-01', 'nb-m2', 'module', 0, 1, 'Which device primarily forwards packets between networks?', '["Router","Switch","Monitor","Keyboard"]'::jsonb, 0, 'A router connects and forwards traffic between different networks.'),
  ('nb2-02', 'nb-m2', 'module', 0, 1, 'What is the main job of an Ethernet switch?', '["Provide a video display","Connect wired devices within a LAN","Write Wi-Fi passwords","Translate websites into books"]'::jsonb, 1, 'A switch interconnects wired devices on a local network.'),
  ('nb2-03', 'nb-m2', 'module', 0, 1, 'Which medium usually provides a wired LAN connection?', '["Bluetooth speaker","Printed barcode","Ethernet cable","Camera lens"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Ethernet cabling is a common wired LAN connection method.'),
  ('nb2-04', 'nb-m2', 'module', 1, 2, 'Why might a classroom use a switch as well as a router?', '["Both devices do exactly the same job in every case","The switch replaces every computer","A router can never connect to a switch","The switch connects local wired devices; the router connects networks"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Switches serve local wired connectivity; routers provide network-to-network forwarding.'),
  ('nb2-05', 'nb-m2', 'module', 1, 2, 'Why can Wi-Fi become unreliable through several thick walls?', '["Wireless signals can weaken and encounter interference","Ethernet cables disappear","Wi-Fi becomes a WAN automatically","The router loses its IP permanently"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Distance and barriers can reduce wireless signal quality.'),
  ('nb2-06', 'nb-m2', 'module', 1, 2, 'How can one home gateway serve as a router, switch, and access point?', '["Every home contains three hidden computers","It can combine several networking functions in one device","Switching is impossible on routers","It uses no network interfaces"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Consumer gateways frequently integrate several networking functions.'),
  ('nb2-07', 'nb-m2', 'module', 2, 2, 'A desktop has an Ethernet port and sits beside a switch. Which connection is sensible?', '["HDMI cable to the internet provider","USB charger to the wall","Ethernet cable from desktop to switch","Audio cable to the router"]'::jsonb, 2, 'An Ethernet cable carries wired network traffic.'),
  ('nb2-08', 'nb-m2', 'module', 2, 2, 'A phone needs wireless access to a school LAN. Which component provides the wireless entry point?', '["Printer toner","Ethernet-only patch cable","Monitor","Wireless access point"]'::jsonb, 3, 'An access point lets wireless devices join the LAN.'),
  ('nb2-09', 'nb-m2', 'module', 2, 2, 'A house loses power to its Wi-Fi router. What is the first sensible action?', '["Check that the router has power and restart only when appropriate","Change every website password","Replace all phones","Reinstall every web browser"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Start by verifying the affected equipment is powered and functioning.'),
  ('nb2-10', 'nb-m2', 'module', 3, 3, 'Wired computers work, but tablets cannot join Wi-Fi. Where should you investigate first?', '["Every Ethernet cable must be broken","Wireless access point or Wi-Fi settings","The printer tray","The keyboard layout"]'::jsonb, 1, 'A wireless-specific fault is more likely when wired access still works.'),
  ('nb2-11', 'nb-m2', 'module', 3, 3, 'An Ethernet PC shows no link light while nearby PCs work. What is the best initial check?', '["Assume the entire internet is offline","Delete the operating system","Check that its cable is firmly connected and try a known-good port or cable","Change the website URL"]'::jsonb, 2, 'A single failed wired link suggests checking its local cable or port.'),
  ('nb2-12', 'nb-m2', 'module', 3, 3, 'A team needs reliable connectivity for fixed desktop PCs and mobility for tablets. What is the best design?', '["Wi-Fi only for every device without exception","No router and no access point","Separate internet subscription per tablet","Ethernet for desktops and Wi-Fi for tablets on the same LAN"]'::jsonb, 3, 'A combined wired and wireless LAN matches the different device needs.'),
  ('nb3-01', 'nb-m3', 'module', 0, 1, 'What does IP stand for in IP address?', '["Internet Protocol","Internal Printer","Internet Program","Input Port"]'::jsonb, 0, 'IP is short for Internet Protocol.'),
  ('nb3-02', 'nb-m3', 'module', 0, 1, 'What does DNS commonly help a device find?', '["The monitor brightness","An IP address associated with a domain name","A Wi-Fi password","An Ethernet cable color"]'::jsonb, 1, 'DNS resolves names to records such as IP addresses.'),
  ('nb3-03', 'nb-m3', 'module', 0, 1, 'What is a packet in networking?', '["A type of printer paper","A Wi-Fi password","A unit of data sent across a network","A physical router"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Packets are units used to carry data over networks.'),
  ('nb3-04', 'nb-m3', 'module', 1, 2, 'Why use domain names rather than require people to memorize numeric addresses?', '["Names eliminate the need for network addresses","DNS turns a computer into a router","Domains automatically prevent phishing","Names are easier for people to remember, and DNS helps locate destinations"]'::jsonb, 3, 'DNS makes human-readable names usable for reaching services.'),
  ('nb3-05', 'nb-m3', 'module', 1, 2, 'What is the role of IP addressing when data travels?', '["It helps network equipment direct data toward an intended destination","It changes every document into a photo","It supplies electricity to Wi-Fi","It replaces all application protocols"]'::jsonb, 0, 'IP addresses help identify destinations for routed traffic.'),
  ('nb3-06', 'nb-m3', 'module', 1, 2, 'Why is opening a webpage more than simply "using DNS"?', '["DNS already contains all web pages","DNS assists name resolution; connections and data transfers are still required","No packets are used on the internet","The keyboard sends the whole page"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Resolving the domain is only one stage in accessing a website.'),
  ('nb3-07', 'nb-m3', 'module', 2, 2, 'A learner sees 192.168.1.25 in device settings. What is it likely to represent?', '["A domain name","A Wi-Fi password","A private IPv4 address","An Ethernet cable model"]'::jsonb, 2, '192.168.x.x is within a commonly used private IPv4 range.'),
  ('nb3-08', 'nb-m3', 'module', 2, 2, 'A site is entered as example.com. Which service is normally consulted to learn its address?', '["Bluetooth pairing service","Print spooler","Screen saver","DNS resolver"]'::jsonb, 3, 'DNS is used for domain-name resolution.'),
  ('nb3-09', 'nb-m3', 'module', 2, 2, 'Which sequence best describes simplified website access?', '["Resolve name, connect to server, request content, receive content","Print page, then enable cable, then invent a domain","Request content without any network, then resolve name","Change password, then power off router"]'::jsonb, 0, 'A web request generally uses name resolution and network communication.'),
  ('nb3-10', 'nb-m3', 'module', 3, 3, 'A browser says a domain cannot be resolved, but other network checks succeed. What should you test?', '["Only the monitor cable","DNS settings and resolver availability","Printer ink level","Mouse battery"]'::jsonb, 1, 'A name resolution error points toward DNS-related checks.'),
  ('nb3-11', 'nb-m3', 'module', 3, 3, 'A device has a private IP but no working default gateway for reaching outside networks. What is the likely impact?', '["All local printers must automatically fail","Its keyboard becomes disabled","Local LAN traffic may work while internet destinations fail","DNS names disappear from the web"]'::jsonb, 2, 'A gateway is needed for forwarding traffic beyond the local network.'),
  ('nb3-12', 'nb-m3', 'module', 3, 3, 'A learner claims an IP address always identifies a particular person. Which response is best?', '["IP addresses are legal names","All phones share one permanent public IP","IP addresses cannot change","An IP address identifies network connectivity and is not, by itself, proof of a specific person"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Addresses identify network endpoints or interfaces, not reliably individual people.'),
  ('nb4-01', 'nb-m4', 'module', 0, 1, 'Which is a recommended Wi-Fi security option when supported?', '["WPA3","No password","Open access for everyone","Posting the password publicly"]'::jsonb, 0, 'WPA3 is a modern Wi-Fi security option.'),
  ('nb4-02', 'nb-m4', 'module', 0, 1, 'What does troubleshooting mean?', '["Replacing every device immediately","Systematically identifying and resolving a problem","Turning off all security settings","Guessing passwords repeatedly"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Troubleshooting is a structured process for narrowing down causes.'),
  ('nb4-03', 'nb-m4', 'module', 0, 1, 'What does HTTPS generally help protect?', '["A router from power failure","Every site from being fraudulent","Data exchanged with a website in transit","A computer from all malware"]'::jsonb, 2, 'HTTPS encrypts web traffic in transit but does not guarantee a site is trustworthy.'),
  ('nb4-04', 'nb-m4', 'module', 1, 2, 'Why compare a second device on the same Wi-Fi network?', '["To improve screen resolution","To delete saved files","To increase modem size","To determine whether the issue is device-specific or network-wide"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Comparison helps determine the likely scope of the fault.'),
  ('nb4-05', 'nb-m4', 'module', 1, 2, 'Why is a strong Wi-Fi password useful?', '["It reduces unauthorized access to the wireless network","It makes the internet free","It prevents every scam message","It guarantees perfect signal strength"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Strong authentication helps restrict access to trusted users.'),
  ('nb4-06', 'nb-m4', 'module', 1, 2, 'Why is a padlock icon not enough to prove a site is legitimate?', '["A padlock indicates no encryption","HTTPS encrypts the connection but scammers can also use HTTPS","All HTTPS sites are government sites","Wi-Fi must be switched off"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Encryption and website legitimacy are different security questions.'),
  ('nb4-07', 'nb-m4', 'module', 2, 2, 'A learner finds two similar Wi-Fi names in a cafe. What should they do?', '["Choose the one with the most suspicious login page","Use both at once","Ask staff to verify the official network before connecting","Share their password to test it"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Verify the network name to reduce the risk of an impersonating hotspot.'),
  ('nb4-08', 'nb-m4', 'module', 2, 2, 'Only one laptop cannot connect but all other devices can. What should be checked first?', '["The internet service for the entire country","Every other student''s passwords","Replace the provider network","The laptop''s Wi-Fi status, selected network, and saved settings"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Begin by investigating the single affected device.'),
  ('nb4-09', 'nb-m4', 'module', 2, 2, 'A learner receives a browser warning about an invalid certificate. What is safest?', '["Do not bypass the warning for sensitive activity; verify the site and connection","Enter passwords anyway","Disable browser security permanently","Assume the warning is always a joke"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Certificate errors require verification, especially before sharing sensitive information.'),
  ('nb4-10', 'nb-m4', 'module', 3, 3, 'All devices lose internet but can still print locally. What is the best initial diagnosis?', '["Every printer must be broken","Local LAN works; examine gateway or internet service","Every device has the same virus","Wi-Fi passwords must all be wrong"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Local function plus widespread internet failure points upstream.'),
  ('nb4-11', 'nb-m4', 'module', 3, 3, 'A router restart does not restore access and the provider reports an outage. What should users do?', '["Keep changing random security settings","Factory-reset all devices immediately","Record the outage and use a trusted alternative if needed","Disable Wi-Fi encryption"]'::jsonb, 2, 'An external service outage is not corrected by random local configuration changes.'),
  ('nb4-12', 'nb-m4', 'module', 3, 3, 'Which troubleshooting strategy produces the clearest evidence?', '["Change passwords, DNS, router, and cables simultaneously","Skip checking whether all devices are affected","Assume the first guess is correct","Test one variable at a time and note outcomes"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Controlled checks help isolate causes and avoid introducing new faults.')
on conflict (id) do update set question_text = excluded.question_text, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, difficulty = excluded.difficulty;

